  {
   "instrument_id": "EO:6513K",
   "outcome": "blocked",
   "reason": "[\"EO 6513-K amends only the seventh paragraph of Article I of the automobile code (the expiration date), moving it from December 31, 1933 to September 4, 1934, 'effective immediately'. Held EO 6837 (August 31, 1934) recites that paragraph as it stood after this order and replaces it, 'effective immediately', so the wording this order enacted ceased to be the code's text on August 31, 1934 and the first end of this clause is that replacement, not the June 14, 1935 repeal.\",\"The dossier registers no later-event or ending evidence id for EO 6837 (its chain is empty and the order is not an excerpt in the packet), so the ending instrument cannot be cited in a claim; the replacement needs a registered source before this order can be submitted.\"]"
  },
  {
   "instrument_id": "EO:6543M",
   "outcome": "blocked",
   "reason": "[\"Condition (1) stays the code 'in respect to the manufacture and sale of vestees, gilets and guimpes' pending a public hearing on a code for the women's neckwear and scarf industries and the Administrator's determination whether those goods fall under the Blouse and Skirt code; searches of the held corpus found no record of the hearing or of the determination, so whether and when the stay ended before June 14, 1935 is not established.\",\"The direction that the Administrator, after the hearing, shall determine whether the goods are included and incorporate his determination in the code is a further command to an official with no held end; a bounded interval cannot be claimed because it is not established that the determination occurred.\"]"
  },
